        "commit": {
          "author": {
            "date": "2026-08-05T12:55:21Z",
            "email": "rmalone1097@gmail.com",
            "name": "Robert Malone"
          },
          "comment_count": 0,
          "committer": {
            "date": "2026-08-05T12:55:21Z",
            "email": "rmalone1097@gmail.com",
            "name": "Robert Malone"
          },
          "message": "Gate version lockstep locally, not only at the release tag\n\npublish.yml's verify-versions job was the only place that checked core\nversion == cruxible-client version == kit manifest version, with core's\ndependency pin exact. The first thing that could see a break was therefore a\npushed tag: v0.3.1 was tagged with cruxible-client still at 0.3.0 and the\npublish failed at the gate.\n\nExtract the check into scripts/check_version_lockstep.py (stdlib only, since\nverify-versions runs on a bare checkout with no install), have the workflow\ninvoke it with --tag, and add it to scripts/ci_parity.sh without one - a local\ntree has no release tag, but every other relationship is checkable pre-push.\nThe script reports every violation rather than raising on the first, so one\nrun shows the whole stamping state.",
          "tree": {
